hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  I believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow a business is sum  all of the strategies of people who have  already done what you're trying to do so  today we're gonna look at how a man who  started a website as a part-time hobby  and had no formal business plan went on  to create one of the top ten websites in  the world this is a story of Craigslist  founder Craig Newmark and the top three  lessons you can learn from his success  Craig Newmark is an American  entrepreneur that started with an idea  to inform people to turn in the  Craigslist a multi-million dollar  internet business Newmark grew up in  Morristown New Jersey his father a  salesman who peddled everything from  food to insurance died of lung cancer  shortly after Newmark's Bar Mitzvah his  mother worked as a bookkeeper and  struggled to make ends meet after her  husband passed away Newmark went to  Marston High School where he became  co-captain of the debate team and also  an active member of the forensics Club  he also started his own Club which might  regularly the play the game go a few  years after graduating college Newmark  worked at IBM in Florida then for  Charles Schwab in San Francisco Newark  then began working as an independent  consultant taking on contracts with Bank  of America Sun Microsystems and more  after several years of observing people  on the internet and how they used online  tools to help each other out new Merck  decided to start his own email service  to notify people about cool arts and  technology events in San Francisco when  you mark simple email listing reached  over two hundred and forty subscribers  he could no longer carry on as he was  even his CC field would not accept any  more email addresses instead of shutting  down new mark decided to move his list  to a public server for all to access he  wanted to call his new website SF events  for San Francisco events but some of his  closest friend suggested cullinan  Craigslist to emphasize the personal and  down the earth nature of the list in his  first few years new mark ran the site as  a part-time hobby in continuing his  consulting work full-time during the day  he tried to bring on some volunteers but  they didn't pan out as Newmark expected  this is when he had an epiphany he hired  the right CEO and Craigslist took off  practices earning over ten million  dollars in revenues for 2004 then in  2005 for price tag of 15 million dollars  eBay purchased a 25% stake in a company  from a former shareholder as of 2010  Craigslist was generating more than one  hundred and twenty-two million dollars  annually by following his passion and  recognizing that he couldn't do  everything himself Craig Newmark was  able to turn his business from a  part-time hobby into a globally  recognized brand to help you explode  your business here are three action  items and you can learn from Craig  Newmark actually not a number one get  out of the way a huge challenge for many  entrepreneurs is recognizing what you  should and should not be doing in your  business focus your time and energy on  the tasks that you bring the most amount  of value to and delegate or outsource  the rest if you hang on the control of  every task you'll always be limited in  how much your business can grow because  you won't have enough time one of the  reasons why Craigslist has become such a  success story is because Newmark has  understood the importance of getting out  of the way where and when it mattered  from content to the overall management  of the site he knew that it was not  going to be him who always had the best  answers and when it counted he was  willing to step back and hand over the  reins even though he was getting a lot  of interest from IT venture capitalist  Newmark awaited the amongst refusal to  bring on a partner was not a power grab  he would hand over the reins where and  when it felt right and that time came in  2000 when he decided to promote  entrepreneur Jim buck master as CEO  that's when the company really began to  take off he knew he needed someone  better than himself and decided to get  out of the way according to new mark  frankly as a manager I kind of suck  but fortunately Jim didn't he's a much  better manager than I am and because the  guy who started a company is not always  the right guy to lead it into the future  people that start companies and lack  management skills they fail getting  another way is really important we  didn't care that the site wasn't being  used how we had a match  the Internet is about inclusion on the  net no one should feel left out action  item number to do things better to reach  success as an entrepreneur you need to  do things differently and better than  your competition you don't need to be  better at everything pick something you  can be really good at and be the best at  it  customers who care about that feature  will come to you being average at  everything is a recipe for failure being  good at a few things that your customers  really care about or rocking your  success forward the good thing about not  having an adventure capitalist backing  him meant that Newmark was free to do  what he wanted with his company he was  free to innovate or to step back and let  his user to innovate for him one of his  inventions came in the form of the best  of Craigslist blog  ideally rounded with the craziest most  hilarious postings that are left by  users on the site knew mark who enjoys  sifting through the online discussions  on a daily basis pulls out the funniest  and most ludicrous posting some across  the Craigslist network and compiles him  into a daily blog by letting users post  this kind of stuff new mark was able to  build readership and loyalty to the site  having the ability to innovate a lot of  trick less to do things better Gordon  and Newmark were innovative in many  small ways when we see something that  could be done better we do it this is  the notion of Kaizen the Japanese  practice of continuous business process  re-engineering people can see that when  they report a problem to us  we take it seriously we want life to be  fair even though it's not sometimes you  got to be fast so you don't waste the  time of others action of them number  three listen no matter how great a  product or service you have you'll  always have to make changes based on  what your prospects and customers say  encourage their feedback  better yet start talking to them before  you even have a product or service ready  to sell build it around their needs  there's nothing like creating the  business around paying customers to  ensure that you get past the survival  stage and go on to build a highly  successful company from its onset  Craigslist was born from the ideas and  suggestions of his users when Newmark  began sending on his email list in 1995  to a small group of interested  subscribers almost immediately he began  receiving emails back with suggestions  for job and apartment listing  they hope Newmark would add to his list  recognizing importance of a feedback  loop has been crucial for the success of  the small company in fact that has come  to represent one of its founding  corporate values and one of the reasons  why millions of people the world over  continue to turn to their local  Craigslist for help and making many of  their most important life decisions to  this day Newmark spends six hours of  every working day on customer service  responding to the needs and requests of  his users according to new mark from the  very beginning I was involved in talking  to people listening to people and it  hasn't stopped the idea that people send  me information I'd asked him about it  listen try to do something about it and  then ask for more feedback community  people let me know that the volunteer  operation was failing and help me get  out of denial 90% of the function of our  site is based on suggestions from users  so remember get out of the way do things  better and listen to finish up this  video I wanted to share what my favorite  true stories about Craig Newmark and  some of his best quotes  despite his professional successes  Newmark struggled personally he enrolled  in ballet and jazz dance classes in  order to meet women willing to wind up  in the hospital with a hernia no matter  what most people say one of the biggest  reasons Newmark started Craigslist was  because of his struggling personal life  he is a self-admitted nerd which really  turned off women he thought it was a  good idea to start helping people by  starting an email service for others  like himself after finally getting too  many people using his email service  Newmark started Craigslist according to  him it's the reason he has the  girlfriend he has today he likes to say  that Craigslist has prevented hurting  himself just to meet women out of this  struggle for personal contact Newmark  built one of the top 10 websites in the  world according to recent stats more  than 5 million people use a site every  month and more than 1 billion pages of  Craigslist are looked at every month  thank you for joining me for another  edition of mauling the Masters if you  liked the video and you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up it helps let  me know that you guys like the videos  and I also love to hear what you have to  think if you want to leave a comment  under the video and thank you and we'll  see you on the next episode  you
 

